.TH STRING 3 "2026" "y-- standard library" "y-- Value Types"
.SH NAME
string \- built-in string value type methods
.SH DESCRIPTION
Strings in y-- are mutable sequences of characters. They support a wide range of
built-in methods for manipulation, searching, formatting, and functional programming.
.SH "CORE METHODS"
.TP
\fBappend(str)\fR -> string()
Appends the contents of \fBstr\fR to the end of the string in-place.
.TP
\fBreserve(size)\fR -> none()
Pre-allocates memory for the string up to \fBsize\fR characters to avoid reallocations.
.TP
\fBresize(size)\fR -> none()
Resizes the string buffer to \fBsize\fR.
.TP
\fBreverse([modify_original=true, custom_lambda=None])\fR -> string()
Reverses the string. If \fBmodify_original\fR is true, modifies the string in-place.
If a \fBcustom_lambda\fR is provided, it is applied to each character before reversing.
.TP
\fBsort([reverse_sort=false, modify_original=true, custom_lambda=None])\fR -> string()
Sorts the characters in the string based on ASCII values, or by using a \fBcustom_lambda\fR.
.SH "TRANSFORMATIONS & FORMATTING"
.TP
\fBcapitalize([modify_original=true])\fR -> string()
Capitalizes the first character of the string.
.TP
\fBcasefold([modify_original=true])\fR -> string()
Converts to a lowercase form suitable for caseless matching.
.TP
\fBcenter(width, [fillchar=' ', modify_original=true])\fR -> string()
Centers the string within a given \fBwidth\fR using \fBfillchar\fR.
.TP
\fBchars([start=0, end=-1])\fR -> list()
Returns a list of single-character strings.
.TP
\fBsplit([delimiter=" "])\fR -> list()
Splits the string into a list of strings by the specified \fBdelimiter\fR.
.TP
\fBljust(width, [fillchar, modify_original])\fR, \fBrjust(...)\fR -> string()
Left-justifies or right-justifies the string within a field of size \fBwidth\fR.
.TP
\fBlower([modify_original=true])\fR, \fBupper([modify_original=true])\fR -> string()
Converts the string to entirely lowercase or uppercase characters.
.SH "WHITESPACE & STRIPPING"
.TP
\fBstrip([chars=" \\t\\n\\r\\v\\f", modify_original=true])\fR -> string()
Removes leading and trailing characters that match \fBchars\fR.
.TP
\fBlstrip(...)\fR, \fBrstrip(...)\fR -> string()
Removes leading or trailing characters, respectively.
.SH "SEARCHING & QUERYING"
.TP
\fBascii()\fR -> int()
Returns the ASCII integer value for a string of length 1.
.TP
\fBcount(sub, [start=0, end=-1])\fR -> int()
Returns the number of non-overlapping occurrences of \fBsub\fR.
.TP
\fBendswith(suffix)\fR -> bool()
Returns true if the string ends with \fBsuffix\fR.
.TP
\fBindex(sub)\fR -> int()
Returns the starting index of the first occurrence of \fBsub\fR.
.TP
\fBisalnum()\fR, \fBisalpha()\fR, \fBisdecimal()\fR, \fBislower()\fR, \fBisupper()\fR -> bool()
Returns true if all characters in the string match the respective property.
.SH "FUNCTIONAL METHODS"
Strings can be iterated over as collections of single characters.
.TP
\fBAll_Of / Any_Of / None_Of / One_Of (lambda)\fR -> bool()
Evaluates a boolean condition over all characters.
.TP
\fBselect / reject (lambda)\fR -> string()
Filters characters keeping those that return true/false, re-joining them into a string.
.TP
\fBmap(lambda)\fR -> string()|list()
Maps each character. Returns a string if all mapped elements are strings, otherwise a list.
.SH "SEE ALSO"
list(3), Math(3)
